# Shell scripts run under bash on the build machines and must keep LF endings in every working copy.
# Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) turns them into CRLF, and an EAS build uploaded
# from that checkout fails in the post-install hook: "$'\r': command not found", then "syntax error
# near unexpected token `fi'" (Android preview build 4dc34648, 2026-11-21).
*.sh text eol=lf
